{
  "season": "2026 – 2027",
  "intro": "Train with ICCD and dive into the heart of Cuban folklore. Led by former masters of the Conjunto Folklórico Nacional de Cuba, these weekends are a rare chance to go deep into Afro-Cuban dance and music with live percussion and chants. More than a workshop, it is a full cultural immersion.",
  "level": "These trainings are designed for intermediate to advanced dancers looking for meaningful growth and a deeper connection to Cuban folkloric dance and music. They are not beginner classes: a basic knowledge of Yoruba, Arará, Palo, Makuta, Yuka and Rumba is expected.",
  "included": [
    "10 hours of classes over 2 days (Saturday & Sunday)",
    "Afro-Cuban dance and chants: Yoruba, Arará, Palo, Makuta, Yuka, Rumba",
    "Live music: batá, tambor, güiro and vocals",
    "Cuban popular dances: Son, Mambo, Cha-cha-chá and more",
    "The methodology of Cuba's top folkloric school"
  ],
  "scheduleNote": "Trainings usually start on Saturday around noon and finish around 5 pm on Sunday. The full class schedule is published one week before each training.",
  "reminders": [
    "Please be on time, we recommend arriving 10 minutes early",
    "Store your personal belongings in the locker rooms",
    "Remove outdoor shoes before entering the dance room",
    "Respect the line structure as presented by the direction",
    "Eat before class",
    "Wear proper training clothes",
    "Bring your dance accessories (heels, skirts…)",
    "Don't forget to bring water!",
    "Schedules might be subject to changes"
  ],
